cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the digit readers, please cite it as below."
title: "STC Studio and neural networks in 8051 assembly"
abstract: >-
  An 8051 assembler that produces Keil's bytes, a cycle-accurate simulator of the STC89C52RC board, a Web Serial
  programmer, and multilayer perceptrons for handwritten digit recognition in 8051 assembly with the generator that
  writes them, the C versions for Keil C51 and SDCC, and the scripts behind the paper "Extreme Edge AI: Neural
  Network Digit Recognition in 8051 Assembly".
authors:
  - family-names: "Merchán-Cruz"
    given-names: "Emmanuel"
    affiliation: "Transport and Telecommunication Institute"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eamcmx/stc-studio"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-08
keywords:
  - 8051
  - STC89C52RC
  - assembler
  - simulator
  - TinyML
  - neural network
